+  <tr><td>Transfer</td><td>Per-surface sizing</td><td>grid 320px 4:3 vs avatar 160px 1:1</td><td>Where most of the "our images are huge" problem actually lives</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Transfer</td><td><code>maxRequestsPerHost = 12</code></td><td>OkHttp <code>Dispatcher</code></td><td>Default is <strong>5 per host</strong>; a CDN is one host, so tile 6 waits on tile 1 while the radio idles</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Transfer</td><td>Warm connection pool</td><td>8 idle / 5 min keep-alive</td><td>A TLS handshake costs more than a 15 KB WebP</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Caching</td><td>Immutable content-addressed URLs</td><td><code>max-age=1y, immutable</code></td><td>No invalidation problem, ever</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Caching</td><td>Shared cache key discipline</td><td><code>VariantResolver</code> is the only producer</td><td>Prefetch and display provably agree; otherwise prefetch is pure waste</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Caching</td><td>Never downgrade a decoded image</td><td>per-image richest-variant ledger + residency check</td><td>Leaving WiFi must not re-fetch the viewport at lower quality</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Memory</td><td>Cache budget as a share of heap</td><td>12 / 20 / 25% by tier, <code>maxSize</code> mutable</td><td>25% of a 96 MB heap starves the rest of the app</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Memory</td><td>Hardware bitmaps by default</td><td>Coil <code>allowHardware</code>, API 26+</td><td>Pixels live outside the Java heap entirely</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Memory</td><td>Far-prefetch without decoding</td><td><code>BlackholeDecoder</code> + memory cache off</td><td>Bytes cached, zero bitmaps, no eviction of near images</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Render</td><td>Aspect ratio from the payload</td><td><code>Modifier.aspectRatio(dish.aspectRatio)</code></td><td>Arriving bitmaps never re-trigger layout for the rest of the grid</td></tr>
